#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""sheep — sessionpipe on this Mac, with the vault gated out. Stdlib, Python 3.9.

    sheep gate [--dry-run] [--no-sink | --sink]  gate every sessionpipe hook entry, forget private sessions, then write the sink
    sheep check                     gated / ungated / absent per settings file, the sinks, the outbox, config.json,
                                    the control daemon
    sheep control [--dry-run] [--folder DIR]...
                                    control.json's folders (every repo bar the private ones) and name (this Mac's
                                    sessions' machine); unpaired, it prints the pair line for the owner; refuses a private folder
    sheep forget-private [--dry-run]  ask every sink to delete a private session found in the outbox
    sheep audit                     read-only: every session on spacesheep.dev whose cwd is private (exit 1 on one)
    sheep receiver-check            is there a sessionpipe receiver to run on the home server yet?
    sheep receiver                  not built: step 7 (E4) writes it once receiver-check passes
    sheep url <url>...              each spacesheep link at the local mirror's address when one runs, else as given

Design: docs/record/orchestration-proposal-2026-10-02.md, E1 (section 9) and D1 (section 13): sessionpipe
at tier 2 to spacesheep from both Macs, the vault, the transcript archive, the guarded repos and
Drive's _secrets never leaving. The gate itself is hooks/sheep_gate.py, which also holds the one
definition of "private" (PRIVATE_REPOS); this verb wires it in and keeps it wired. The chart is
docs/sheep.md.

What `check` holds (exit 1 on any): every entry gated in every login dir; no private session in
the outbox; any http(s) sink is exactly one — spacesheep.dev, unpaused, at an effective tier (its
tier, capped by the receiver's max_tier) of 2 or less; config.json's update_check false (gate writes
it and `machine` on their own, before the forget and the sink, so neither a refusal nor a missing
key leaves them unset). It names, without failing, a `machine` other than this Mac's board name,
and notes, counted in its first line and shown by bootstrap.sh even when it passes: no http sink
at all (nothing leaves, nothing reaches the board — the R2 phase), the R2 day's file
(r2-review.jsonl) still on disk, and a control daemon that logged `refused (mode)` since its last
start (0.5.0: one failed `claude --help` read refuses every headless turn after it;
`launchctl kickstart -k gui/$(id -u)/org.sessionpipe.control` restarts it). `audit` pages
`spacesheep sessions list` (100 a page, the CLI's cap) — the board holds both Macs' sessions, so
it is the one place a leak from either shows; it never deletes (`sessionpipe forget` is the owner's).

What sessionpipe does that this works around (its 0.5.0 source, read 2026-10-03):
- `sessionpipe install` writes one entry per event into every Claude config dir's settings.json
  (~/.claude, $CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR, and each ~/.claude[-_.]* holding projects/ or settings.json)
  with the command `"<data>/sessionpipe-hook" claude-code <Event>`, and recognises its own
  entries by a regex anchored at the END of the command. So the gated form
  `python3 "<sheep_gate.py>" "<data>/sessionpipe-hook" claude-code <Event>` is still "ours" to
  sessionpipe: `uninstall` removes it cleanly, and `install`/`update` replace it with the
  ungated form (R1) — after either, run `sheep gate` at once. `sync.py` names an ungated entry
  at every session start, and `gate` runs `forget-private` before it writes the sink.
- **`sessionpipe status` and `doctor` call every gated file "stale"** (they want the exact entry
  they write) and `doctor` says to run `sessionpipe install` again — the one command that
  removes the gate. "stale" is the gate working: never answer it with `install`.
- **A session's title on spacesheep is the one the VS Code panel shows**: the worker reads the
  transcript's `custom-title` (a rename) over its `ai-title` (Claude Code's own), and falls back
  to the first prompt only when neither exists — nothing to configure. Not "none first-ask" any
  more, as 2026-10-07's 60 outbox sessions read: the board on 2026-10-16 held 907 sessions, 545
  titled — 42 of those by the first ask — and 362 untitled. The gate facts below (CLAUDE_EVENTS,
  the OURS regex, wantsTranscript, forget) were re-read unchanged on sessionpipe 0.7.0's source
  the same day (the inventory's reading; this Mac still runs 0.5.0).
- **Backfill does not pass through the gate**: it reads ~/.claude/projects directly and queues a
  `session.backfill` row (cwd, title) for every session of the last N days, the vault's
  included. A bare `sessionpipe install` backfills 30 days. So: always `install --backfill 0`,
  never `sessionpipe backfill`; `forget-private` finds and deletes such rows from the outbox.
- An install with no sink above tier 0 is "lean": it skips PreToolUse and PostToolUseFailure.
  `gate` adds every missing event of EVENTS in gated form, its command copied from an entry
  sessionpipe wrote (read back, never predicted), the shape sessionpipe's own: matcher "" on
  tool and permission events, timeout 5, PermissionRequest 130. So the sink can follow the
  install and no second install — no ungated window — is ever needed.
- Sinks live in sessionpipe's config.json (0600; $SESSIONPIPE_CONFIG, else
  $XDG_CONFIG_HOME|~/.config/sessionpipe/config.json). `sessionpipe sink add --token` would put
  the token on a command line, so `gate` writes the sink there itself: name `spacesheep.dev`,
  https://spacesheep.dev, tier 2 (its well-known says max_tier 2, bearer auth). The token is
  SPACESHEEP_SESSIONS_KEY, a Sessions-only key: the environment, else this repo's .env
  (anchored on this script; else <overlay>/.env) with `the overlay.<host>.env` beside its
  target winning, parsed by bin/secrets' own reader. It is never printed. With no key the sink
  is left alone and said so. `gate` writes no sink while an entry is ungated, the gate file is
  missing, or a private session is still in the outbox. It sets two more keys first, in a write of their own
  (2026-10-16): `update_check: false` — from 0.6 sessionpipe updates its own daemon and re-runs
  `install`, which ungates every entry (R1), and that flag is the one switch that stops it — and
  `machine` (the laptop / the build Mac from hooks/common.py's host_name(), else that name itself): unset,
  sessionpipe names the Mac by os.hostname(), a DHCP name whenever the network hands one out
  (`Mac-225` and `Mac-129` split the board).
- `--no-sink` is step 8's first run (R2: a day of tier-2 events read here before anything
  leaves). With no tier-2 sink sessionpipe never builds a transcript event at all
  (`wantsTranscript`, cli.js 0.5.0), so a sinkless outbox shows no turn text to read: instead
  `--no-sink` writes R2_SINK, a `file:` sink at tier 2 into sessionpipe's state dir — local, the
  day's events go into that JSONL. It refuses while an unpaused http(s) sink exists (that one
  sends regardless). While R2_SINK is there a plain `gate` stays local too — sync.py's "run
  sheep gate" must not ship early — and only `gate --sink` writes the spacesheep sink, dropping
  R2_SINK in the same write and removing the file it wrote (a day of turn text, which
  sessionpipe's file sink leaves 0644).
- `sessionpipe forget claude-code <id>` sends `session.forgotten` to every unpaused sink, prints
  `✗ <sink>` for a refusal, and deletes the outbox file either way, exit 0. So success here is
  "no ✗ and no paused sink"; an id is written to `sheep-forget-pending.json` in sessionpipe's
  state dir before the call and leaves it only on success, so a refused forget is retried.
- The reference receiver: npm `sessionpipe-receiver` 0.5.0 is a placeholder whose CLI prints
  "this command lands in a later milestone", and ghcr.io/micmmakarov/sessionpipe-receiver
  refuses an anonymous pull (2026-10-03) — R8 has fired; step 7 waits on upstream (W6). Upstream
  moved to the spacesheep-dev org (github.com/spacesheep-dev/sessionpipe), so receiver-check
  probes the image under both names (RECEIVER_IMAGES).

A gated entry whose gate file is missing counts as UNGATED: python3 exits 2 on a missing script,
which erases prompts and blocks every tool. `gate` refuses to write one (the primary checkout
has no hooks/sheep_gate.py until this launches there). settings.json is read, changed and written
under bin/claude-settings' lock, with its backup-first, atomic writer.

Paths (tests override): $SHEEP_GATE (else the regatta main checkout's modules/keel/hooks/sheep_gate.py —
the config dir's `home`, never a worktree that will be removed; since B14a, not the overlay's shim), $SHEEP_SESSIONPIPE (else `sessionpipe` on PATH,
else ~/.local/bin/sessionpipe), $SHEEP_SPACESHEEP (else `spacesheep` on PATH), $SESSIONPIPE_STATE /
$XDG_STATE_HOME for the outbox and the daemon's log, $SHEEP_ENV_FILE for the .env, $SHEEP_HOST.
`sheep control` (docs/session-listen-2026-10-13.md, B1): the folders sessionpipe's control daemon may
run a session in, and its name, kept by a file write the daemon reloads — never by `pair`, which needs
a passkey tap and is the owner's in an attended session (D3; hooks/secrets_guard.py denies it to an agent):
`control` only prints the line. Its notes stand above `cmd_control`. Never `sessionpipe connect`,
`install` or `spacesheep machine on`: each rewrites the gated hook entries.

Tests: hooks/test_hooks.sh, "sheep". $SHEEP_PROJECTS, $SHEEP_LAUNCH_AGENTS and $SHEEP_LAUNCHCTL point
control at a scratch tree.
"""
import datetime as dt
import io
import json
import os
import re
import shlex
import shutil
import subprocess
import sys
import tarfile
import urllib.error
import urllib.request
from importlib.machinery import SourceFileLoader
from pathlib import Path

HERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent
HOME = Path.home()


def _legacy():
    """The overlay's checkout (`REGATTA_LEGACY`, else the config dir's `legacy` file: the core's
    legacy_root, read here without loading the core, as GATE is fixed at import), or None."""
    v = os.environ.get("REGATTA_LEGACY")
    if not v:
        cfg = Path(os.environ.get("REGATTA_CONFIG") or HOME / ".config" / "regatta").expanduser()
        try:
            v = next((l.strip() for l in (cfg / "legacy").read_text(encoding="utf-8-sig").splitlines() if l.strip()), "")
        except (OSError, UnicodeDecodeError):
            v = ""
    return Path(v).expanduser() if v else None


def _home():
    """The regatta main checkout (`REGATTA_HOME`, else the config dir's `home` file), or None: read
    here without loading the core, as _legacy() is. A worktree resolves to its main checkout, as
    dispatch resolves the overlay: `gate` writes this path into every login dir, and a worktree's
    path breaks every hook once /finish removes it (B14a landing review, 2026-10-23)."""
    v = os.environ.get("REGATTA_HOME")
    if not v:
        cfg = Path(os.environ.get("REGATTA_CONFIG") or HOME / ".config" / "regatta").expanduser()
        try:
            v = next((l.strip() for l in (cfg / "home").read_text(encoding="utf-8-sig").splitlines() if l.strip()), "")
        except (OSError, UnicodeDecodeError):
            v = ""
    if not v:
        return None
    p = Path(v).expanduser()
    if (p / ".git").is_file():
        try:
            common = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", str(p), "rev-parse", "--path-format=absolute", "--git-common-dir"],
                                    capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=10).stdout.strip()
        except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
            common = ""
        if common:
            p = Path(common).parent
    return p


# The hook command's path: this module's file in the main checkout (B14a, 2026-10-23: the overlay's shim
# until then), else the file beside this one. `gate` moves an entry behind the shim's path to this one
# (gated()), so a run after the change re-points every settings file it writes.
_HOME = _home()
GATE = Path(os.environ.get("SHEEP_GATE") or next(
    (p for p in [_HOME / "modules" / "keel" / "hooks" / "sheep_gate.py"] if _HOME and p.is_file()),
    HERE.parent / "hooks" / "sheep_gate.py"))
_gate = SourceFileLoader("sheep_gate", str(HERE.parent / "hooks" / "sheep_gate.py")).load_module()

# sessionpipe 0.5.0's CLAUDE_EVENTS, in its order (core/src/adapters/claude-code.ts).
EVENTS = ["SessionStart", "UserPromptSubmit", "PreToolUse", "PostToolUse", "PostToolUseFailure",
          "PermissionRequest", "Notification", "Stop", "SubagentStart", "SubagentStop",
          "PreCompact", "PostCompact", "SessionEnd", "StopFailure"]
# sessionpipe's own test for "an entry we wrote", ported from claude-shaped.ts.
OURS = re.compile(r'(?:sessionpipe[^"\n]*[\\/]hook\.js|[\\/]sessionpipe-hook)"?\s+[a-z][a-z-]*\s+[A-Za-z]+\s*$')
TAIL = re.compile(r"\s+claude-code\s+[A-Za-z]+\s*$")
SINK = {"name": "spacesheep.dev", "url": "https://spacesheep.dev", "tier": 2, "pii": False}
KEY = "SPACESHEEP_SESSIONS_KEY"
KEEP_BACKUPS = 5
# Upstream moved from Misha's account to the spacesheep-dev org (github.com/spacesheep-dev/sessionpipe,
# seen 2026-10-16); an image may appear under either name, so receiver-check probes both.
RECEIVER_IMAGES = ("spacesheep-dev/sessionpipe-receiver", "micmmakarov/sessionpipe-receiver")
RECEIVER_NPM = "sessionpipe-receiver"
# What `gate` keeps in sessionpipe's config.json beside the sink (2026-10-16):
# - update_check false: from 0.6 sessionpipe updates its own daemon and re-runs `install`, which
#   rewrites every entry ungated (R1); config.json's update_check is the one switch that stops it.
# - machine: the board's name for this Mac. Unset, sessionpipe takes os.hostname() (machineName,
#   cli.js 0.5.0), which is the DHCP name whenever the network hands one out — `Mac-225` and
#   `Mac-129` split one Mac on the board. The names are the ones the board and docs already use.
# `keel/machines`, one `<host>:<board name>` per line; a host it does not name shows as itself.
# sessionpipe's control daemon (`sessionpipe connect`, paired 2026-10-14): its log, its start line,
# and the 0.5.0 bug where one failed `claude --help` read refuses every headless turn after it
# ("refused (mode)") until the daemon restarts.
DAEMON_LOG = ("control", "daemon.log")
DAEMON_UP = re.compile(r"\scontrol daemon \S+ up\b")
DAEMON_KICK = "launchctl kickstart -k gui/$(id -u)/org.sessionpipe.control"
AUDIT_PAGE = 100  # the spacesheep CLI refuses --limit above 100 (lib/inspection.js, 1.30.0)
AUDIT_MAX_PAGES = 200
# The spacesheep mirror (CLI 1.27+, `spacesheep mirror on`): spacesheep.dev itself at localhost, so
# a link opens in a VS Code tab (Simple Browser, through the user setting
# "workbench.externalUriOpeners": {"localhost:4280": "simpleBrowser.open"}) instead of Chrome.
# Read from the CLI's lib/mirror.js (spacesheep-cli main, 1.30.0, 2026-10-11): a running mirror
# writes <config>/mirror.json {pid, port, site} and removes it on exit — the CLI's own `deploy`
# reads that file to print a page's local address, so this reads it too rather than probing the
# port (another program on 4280 is not a mirror, and `/` answers only after a round trip to
# spacesheep.dev). The map is the CLI's addressMap: spacesheep.dev/X → localhost:<port>/X,
# <uuid>.spacesheep.app → <uuid>.localhost:<port>. Committed docs keep spacesheep.dev links:
# localhost means nothing on the phone or on GitHub; only what goes into chat is mapped.
SITE_RE = re.compile(r"^https://spacesheep\.dev(?=[/?#]|$)")
APP_RE = re.compile(r"^https://([0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{12})\.spacesheep\.app(?=[/?#]|$)")
LOCAL_RE = re.compile(r"^http://(?:([0-9a-f-]{36})\.)?localhost:(\d+)(?=[/?#]|$)")
FLAGS = {"gate": {"--dry-run", "--no-sink", "--sink"}, "check": set(), "forget-private": {"--dry-run"},
         "audit": set(), "receiver-check": set(), "receiver": set(), "control": {"--dry-run"}}


class Refused(Exception):
    pass


def say(line=""):
    print(line, flush=True)


def _load(name, path):
    return SourceFileLoader(name, str(path)).load_module()


def _common():
    """The regatta core's common.py: host_name(), and tool() for a peer module's file (lib/find_core.py: the checkout this module sits in, else the config dir's `home`, else the plugin's installPath; never a copy). No core is an ImportError the callers' own guards take."""
    # Loaded once: fence_mark and scan() call this per line, and find_core reads the home file
    # and installed_plugins.json each time (1,521 lookups in one `keel open`, review of B4).
    if "common" in sys.modules:
        return sys.modules["common"]
    lib = str(HERE.parent / "lib")
    if lib not in sys.path:
        sys.path.insert(0, lib)
    import find_core
    try:
        hooks = find_core.hooks()
    except SystemExit:
        raise ImportError("sheep: the regatta core is missing")
    if hooks not in sys.path:
        sys.path.insert(0, hooks)
    import common
    return common


def _sheep_cmd():
    """How a message names this tool: the overlay's shim while it has one (its allow rules name it), else this file."""
    p = (_legacy() or HERE.parent) / "bin" / "sheep"
    import pwd
    s = str(p if _legacy() and p.is_file() else Path(__file__).resolve())
    for home in (str(HOME), pwd.getpwuid(os.getuid()).pw_dir):   # the login's own when a suite moved HOME
        if home and s.startswith(home.rstrip("/") + "/"):
            return "~" + s[len(home.rstrip("/")):]
    return s


def _claude_settings():
    """claude-settings' writer and lock (lighthouse's, regatta-modules G11): found through the
    core's tool(); without it the verbs that write settings refuse in one line, and the pages,
    check and audit still read."""
    p = _common().tool("claude-settings")
    if not p:
        raise Refused("claude-settings (lighthouse) is not installed — settings are not written; "
                      "check and audit still read")
    return _load("claude_settings", p)


# --- where things are -------------------------------------------------------------------------

def mirror_port():
    """The running mirror's port, from the CLI's mirror.json when its pid is alive, else None."""
    d = os.environ.get("SPACESHEEP_CONFIG_DIR") or Path(os.environ.get("XDG_CONFIG_HOME") or HOME / ".config") / "spacesheep"
    try:
        s = json.loads((Path(d) / "mirror.json").read_text())
        pid, port, site = int(s["pid"]), int(s["port"]), str(s.get("site") or "https://spacesheep.dev")
    except Exception:  # absent, unreadable or malformed: no mirror
        return None
    if pid <= 0 or site.rstrip("/") != "https://spacesheep.dev":
        return None  # kill(0 or -1) always succeeds; a mirror of another site (a dev server) is not spacesheep.dev
    try:
        # any failure, EPERM included, is "not running", as the CLI's readStatus has it: the mirror
        # runs as this user, so EPERM means a stale file whose pid another user's process now holds
        os.kill(pid, 0)
    except Exception:
        return None
    return port


def local_url(url, port=None):
    """`url` at the local mirror when one runs (or at `port`), else unchanged; non-spacesheep links pass."""
    port = port or mirror_port()
    if not port:
        return url
    m = APP_RE.match(url)
    if m:
        return "http://%s.localhost:%d%s" % (m.group(1), port, url[m.end():])
    m = SITE_RE.match(url)
    return "http://localhost:%d%s" % (port, url[m.end():] or "/") if m else url


def chat_url(url, port=None):
    """`url` as chat hands it to the owner — `sheep url` and memo's chat_page both: local_url, except in
    a Remote Control run (CLAUDE_CODE_ENTRYPOINT=sdk-cli, read on the phone) or an unattended one
    (CLAUDE_UNATTENDED, read by nobody), where localhost opens nothing and the https link stays."""
    if os.environ.get("CLAUDE_UNATTENDED") or os.environ.get("CLAUDE_CODE_ENTRYPOINT") == "sdk-cli":
        return url
    return local_url(url, port)


def web_url(url, port=None):
    """The inverse: an address on the running mirror (or on `port`) back to spacesheep.dev /
    spacesheep.app; anything else unchanged — a localhost link with no mirror behind it is dead,
    and stays a localhost link for the caller to refuse."""
    m = LOCAL_RE.match(url)
    if not m or int(m.group(2)) != (port or mirror_port()):
        return url
    rest = url[m.end():]
    return ("https://%s.spacesheep.app%s" % (m.group(1), rest)) if m.group(1) else "https://spacesheep.dev" + (rest or "/")


def claude_dirs():
    """sessionpipe's own discovery (claudeDirs), so the gate covers every file it writes."""
    out = []
    def add(d):
        if d:
            r = Path(d).expanduser().resolve()
            if r not in out:
                out.append(r)
    add(HOME / ".claude")
    add(os.environ.get("CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR"))
    try:
        for e in sorted(HOME.iterdir()):
            if e.is_dir() and re.match(r"^\.claude[-_.]", e.name) and \
                    ((e / "projects").exists() or (e / "settings.json").exists()):
                add(e)
    except OSError:
        pass
    return [d for i, d in enumerate(out) if i == 0 or d.exists()]


def config_file():
    if os.environ.get("SESSIONPIPE_CONFIG"):
        return Path(os.environ["SESSIONPIPE_CONFIG"]).resolve()
    return Path(os.environ.get("XDG_CONFIG_HOME") or HOME / ".config") / "sessionpipe" / "config.json"


def state_dir():
    if os.environ.get("SESSIONPIPE_STATE"):
        return Path(os.environ["SESSIONPIPE_STATE"]).resolve()
    return Path(os.environ.get("XDG_STATE_HOME") or HOME / ".local" / "state") / "sessionpipe"


def sessionpipe_bin():
    for c in (os.environ.get("SHEEP_SESSIONPIPE"), shutil.which("sessionpipe"),
              str(HOME / ".local" / "bin" / "sessionpipe"), "/opt/homebrew/bin/sessionpipe"):
        if c and os.access(c, os.X_OK):
            return c
    return None


def spacesheep_bin():
    for c in (os.environ.get("SHEEP_SPACESHEEP"), shutil.which("spacesheep"), "/opt/homebrew/bin/spacesheep"):
        if c and os.access(c, os.X_OK):
            return c
    return None


_HOST = []


def host():
    """This Mac's short name, read once per run: common.host_name() spawns scutil, and env_value,
    machine_name and check each ask (review 2026-10-16: about six spawns a gate)."""
    if os.environ.get("SHEEP_HOST"):
        return os.environ["SHEEP_HOST"]
    if not _HOST:
        _HOST.append(_common().host_name())
    return _HOST[0]


def machine_name():
    """This Mac's name on the board: the laptop / the build Mac, else the stable LocalHostName itself."""
    h = host()
    machines = dict(l.split(":", 1) for l in _common().config_lines("keel/machines") or [] if ":" in l)
    return machines.get(h, h)


def kept_settings():
    """The config.json keys `gate` keeps whatever the sink (MACHINES' comment says why)."""
    return {"update_check": False, "machine": machine_name()}


def ensure_kept(dry):
    """Write kept_settings() into config.json on their own, before any sink: a missing key or a
    refused forget must not leave update_check on (review 2026-10-16). Returns a line, or None
    when nothing changes."""
    c = read_config()
    drift = kept_drift(c)
    if not drift:
        return None
    if not dry:
        c.update(kept_settings())
        write_config(c)
        if kept_drift(read_config()):
            raise Refused(f"wrote {config_file()} but a re-read lacks {', '.join(kept_settings())}")
    return f"config: {'would set' if dry else 'set'} {kept_words(drift)}"


def env_value(key):
    """The environment, else the .env (host file first), parsed by bin/secrets' reader."""
    if os.environ.get(key):
        return os.environ[key]
    secrets = _load("secrets_tool", _common().tool("secrets"))  # the core's bin/secrets
    for env in (os.environ.get("SHEEP_ENV_FILE"), _common().CONFIG / "regatta" / ".env", (_legacy() or HERE.parent) / ".env"):
        if not env or not os.path.lexists(str(env)):
            continue
        real = Path(env).resolve()
        files = ([real.with_name(f"{real.stem}.{host()}.env")] if real.suffix == ".env" else []) + [real]
        for f in files:
            if not f.exists():
                continue
            try:
                v = secrets.read_keys(f).get(key)
            except Exception as exc:  # secrets.Fail: offline in Drive, no Full Disk Access
                raise Refused(f"can't read {f.name}: {exc}")
            if v:
                return v
        return None
    return None


# --- settings.json ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

GATED = re.compile(r'^python3 "([^"]*sheep_gate\.py)" ')


def gate_prefix():
    return f'python3 "{GATE}" '


def bare(cmd):
    return GATED.sub("", cmd)


def gated(cmd):
    """The command behind this gate; one behind a gate at another path is moved to this one."""
    return gate_prefix() + bare(cmd)


def is_gated(cmd):
    """Behind this gate, and the gate file is there: a missing script makes python3 exit 2. Behind
    the overlay's shim counts too while that file is there (B14a: `check` stays green on a Mac whose
    settings still name it; `gate` moves them, as it moves any other path). B14b drops the second."""
    if cmd == gated(cmd) and GATE.is_file():
        return True
    m, old = GATED.match(cmd), _legacy()
    shim = old / "hooks" / "sheep_gate.py" if old else None
    return bool(m and shim and Path(m.group(1)) == shim and shim.is_file())


def _cmds(g):
    return [h for h in g.get("hooks") or [] if isinstance(h, dict) and isinstance(h.get("command"), str)]


def ours(group):
    return isinstance(group, dict) and isinstance(group.get("hooks"), list) and \
        any(OURS.search(h["command"]) for h in _cmds(group))


def survey(cfg):
    """{event: "gated" | "ungated" | "absent"} over EVENTS and any other event sessionpipe hooks."""
    hooks = cfg.get("hooks") if isinstance(cfg.get("hooks"), dict) else {}
    out = {ev: "absent" for ev in EVENTS}
    for ev, groups in hooks.items():
        for g in groups if isinstance(groups, list) else []:
            if not ours(g):
                continue
            bad = any(not is_gated(h["command"]) for h in _cmds(g) if OURS.search(h["command"]))
            out[ev] = "ungated" if bad or out.get(ev) == "ungated" else "gated"
    return out


def counts(s):
    return {k: sum(v == k for v in s.values()) for k in ("gated", "ungated", "absent")}


def read_settings(path):
    try:
        raw = path.read_text(encoding="utf-8")
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return None
    cfg = json.loads(raw)
    if not isinstance(cfg, dict):
        raise Refused(f"{path} is not a JSON object — not touched")
    return cfg


def write_settings(cs, path, cfg):
    """bin/claude-settings' writer: a 0600 backup first, atomic, the file's own mode kept, the
    backups pruned to the newest 5 (they hold env values; bootstrap.sh prunes the same glob)."""
    if path.exists():
        cs.write_private(path.with_name(f"{path.name}.bak-{dt.datetime.now():%Y%m%d%H%M%S}"),
                         path.read_bytes())
    cs.write_atomic(path, cfg)
    for old in sorted(path.parent.glob(path.name + ".bak-*"))[:-KEEP_BACKUPS]:
        old.unlink()


def seed_command():
    """sessionpipe's own command, bare and without its `claude-code <Event>` tail, read back from
    the first Claude config dir it hooked; None while it hooked none."""
    for d in claude_dirs():
        try:
            cfg = read_settings(d / "settings.json")
        except (OSError, ValueError, Refused):
            continue
        hooks = cfg.get("hooks") if cfg and isinstance(cfg.get("hooks"), dict) else {}
        for gs in hooks.values():
            for g in gs if isinstance(gs, list) else []:
                for h in _cmds(g) if ours(g) else []:
                    if OURS.search(h["command"]) and TAIL.search(h["command"]):  # claude-code's own, not another adapter's
                        return TAIL.sub("", bare(h["command"]))
    return None


def seed_missing(base):
    """The executable a command runs, when it is not there; checked before any file is written."""
    exe = re.match(r'^"([^"]+)"', base or "")
    return None if exe and Path(exe.group(1)).exists() else (exe.group(1) if exe else base)


def gate_file(path, dry, seed=None):
    """Gate every sessionpipe entry and add the missing events; returns (changes, survey) —
    the survey as the file stands after the write, or as it stands now on a dry run. A file
    sessionpipe never hooked is left alone unless `seed` (seed_command()) is given: a login dir
    made after `sessionpipe install` (a second login dir, 2026-10-06) then gets all of EVENTS, gated,
    without a second install and its ungated window — the file created when the dir holds
    projects/ but no settings.json, as sessionpipe's own install would."""
    if not path.parent.is_dir():
        return [], None  # ~/.claude is in claude_dirs() even when absent: never create it
    cs = _claude_settings()
    with cs.Lock(path.parent):  # the lock claude-settings' apply takes beside this file
        cfg = read_settings(path)
        if cfg is None:
            if not (seed and (path.parent / "projects").is_dir()):
                return [], None
            cfg = {}  # a login dir with sessions but no settings.json yet (bin/account links projects/ only)
        before = survey(cfg)
        if "hooks" in cfg and not isinstance(cfg["hooks"], dict):
            return [], before  # not Claude Code's shape: never overwritten
        hooks = cfg.get("hooks") or {}
        mine = [h["command"] for gs in hooks.values() if isinstance(gs, list)
                for g in gs if ours(g) for h in _cmds(g) if OURS.search(h["command"])]
        if not mine and not seed:
            return [], before  # sessionpipe never hooked any file: nothing of ours to add
        changes = []
        for ev, groups in hooks.items():
            for g in groups if isinstance(groups, list) else []:
                for h in _cmds(g) if ours(g) else []:
                    if OURS.search(h["command"]) and h["command"] != gated(h["command"]):
                        h["command"] = gated(h["command"])
                        changes.append(f"gated {ev}")
        base = TAIL.sub("", bare(mine[0])) if mine else seed  # read back from what sessionpipe wrote
        for ev in EVENTS:
            if not isinstance(hooks.get(ev, []), list):
                continue  # a malformed event value is left as it is
            if not any(ours(g) for g in hooks.get(ev) or []):
                exe = re.match(r'^"([^"]+)"', base)
                if not exe or not Path(exe.group(1)).exists():
                    raise Refused(f"{exe.group(1) if exe else base} is missing — "
                                  "run `sessionpipe install --backfill 0` first")
                e = {"matcher": ""} if re.search(r"Tool|Permission", ev) else {}
                e["hooks"] = [{"type": "command", "command": gated(f"{base} claude-code {ev}"),
                               "timeout": 130 if ev == "PermissionRequest" else 5}]
                hooks.setdefault(ev, []).append(e)
                changes.append(f"added {ev}")
        cfg["hooks"] = hooks
        if not changes or dry:
            return changes, before
        write_settings(cs, path, cfg)
        return changes, survey(read_settings(path))  # the re-read, not the write, is the report


# --- sessionpipe's config.json ----------------------------------------------------------------

def read_config():
    f = config_file()
    if not f.exists():
        return {}
    try:
        c = json.loads(f.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
    except (OSError, ValueError) as exc:
        raise Refused(f"{f} is unreadable ({exc}) — not touched")
    if not isinstance(c, dict):
        raise Refused(f"{f} is not a JSON object — not touched")
    return c


def write_config(c):
    f = config_file()
    f.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True, mode=0o700)
    tmp = f.with_name(f"{f.name}.tmp.{os.getpid()}")
    fd = os.open(tmp, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_TRUNC, 0o600)
    with os.fdopen(fd, "w", encoding="utf-8") as fh:
        fh.write(json.dumps(c, indent=2) + "\n")  # sessionpipe's writeConfig format
    os.chmod(tmp, 0o600)
    os.replace(tmp, f)


def sinks_of(c):
    return [s for s in c.get("sinks") or [] if isinstance(s, dict)]


def ensure_sink(dry):
    token = env_value(KEY)
    if not token:
        return f"sink: {KEY} is empty in .env — no sink written (docs/record/orchestration-proposal-2026-10-02.md, Do this now, item 3)"
    c = read_config()
    sinks = sinks_of(c)
    prev = next((s for s in sinks if s.get("name") == SINK["name"]), None)
    want = dict(prev or {}, **SINK, token=token)
    want.pop("token_in", None)  # a keychain copy would win over the file; the .env is the record
    r2 = any(s.get("name") == "r2-local" for s in sinks)
    if prev == want and not r2:
        return f"sink: {SINK['name']} at tier {SINK['tier']}, already current"
    if not dry:
        c["sinks"] = [s for s in sinks if s.get("name") not in (SINK["name"], "r2-local")] + [want]
        write_config(c)
        if not any(s.get("name") == SINK["name"] and s.get("token") == token for s in sinks_of(read_config())):
            raise Refused(f"wrote {config_file()} but a re-read lacks the sink")
    line = f"sink: {SINK['name']} at tier {SINK['tier']} {'would be ' if dry else ''}{'updated' if prev else 'added'} (token from .env)"
    return line + ("; " + drop_r2_file(dry) if r2 else "")


def kept_drift(c):
    """{key: wanted value} for each of kept_settings() that config.json `c` does not hold yet."""
    return {k: v for k, v in kept_settings().items() if c.get(k) != v}


def kept_words(d):
    return ", ".join(f"{k} {json.dumps(v)}" for k, v in d.items())


def drop_r2_file(dry):
    """The R2 day's events (--no-sink's file sink): gone with the sink that wrote them. Turn text at
    tier 2, left 0644 by sessionpipe's writer (the live one, 2026-10-16) — no reason to keep it."""
    f = Path(r2_sink()["url"][len("file:"):])
    if not f.exists():
        return "r2-local dropped"
    if dry:
        return f"r2-local and {f} would be removed"
    f.unlink()
    return f"r2-local dropped, {f} removed"


def sink_lines():
    out = []
    for s in sinks_of(read_config()):
        tier = effective_tier(s)
        tier = "?" if tier is None else tier
        key = "token in config" if s.get("token") else f"token in {s['token_in']}" if s.get("token_in") else "no token"
        out.append(f"sink {s.get('name')}: {s.get('url')} tier {tier}, {key}" + (f", PAUSED {s['paused']}" if s.get("paused") else ""))
    return out


# --- the outbox ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

def pending_file():
    return state_dir() / "sheep-forget-pending.json"


def read_pending():
    try:
        p = json.loads(pending_file().read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
        return p if isinstance(p, dict) else {}
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return {}


def write_pending(p):
    f = pending_file()
    f.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True, mode=0o700)
    if p:
        f.write_text(json.dumps(p, indent=2) + "\n", encoding="utf-8")
    elif f.exists():
        f.unlink()


def transcript_index():
    """{session id: the folder its transcript is filed under}, over every Claude config dir, the
    first dir winning — built once per call. A glob per outbox file per login dir was most of
    `check`'s 4-8 s with 1,500 outbox files and three login dirs (2026-10-16)."""
    idx = {}
    for d in claude_dirs():
        try:
            folders = [e for e in os.scandir(d / "projects") if e.is_dir()]
        except OSError:
            continue
        for e in folders:
            try:
                names = os.listdir(e.path)
            except OSError:
                continue
            for n in names:
                if n.endswith(".jsonl"):
                    idx.setdefault(n[:-len(".jsonl")], e.name)
    return idx


def private_sessions():
    """[(session id, reason)]: every claude-code outbox file whose session is private, and every
    id a refused forget left pending."""
    base = state_dir() / "outbox" / "claude-code"
    out = dict(read_pending())
    index = None  # built on the first file that needs it: an empty outbox costs no scan
    for f in sorted(base.glob("*.jsonl")) if base.is_dir() else []:
        sid = f.name[:-len(".jsonl")]
        cwd = None
        try:
            with f.open(encoding="utf-8") as fh:
                for line in fh:
                    try:
                        j = json.loads(line)
                    except ValueError:
                        continue
                    s = j.get("session") if isinstance(j, dict) else None
                    cwd = s.get("cwd") if isinstance(s, dict) and isinstance(s.get("cwd"), str) else None
                    if cwd:
                        break
        except OSError:
            continue
        why = _gate.private_reason(cwd=cwd)
        if not why:
            index = transcript_index() if index is None else index
            folder = index.get(sid)
            why = _gate._slug_reason(folder) if folder else None
        if why:
            out.setdefault(sid, why)
    return sorted(out.items())


# --- verbs -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

def r2_sink():
    return {"name": "r2-local", "url": f"file:{state_dir() / 'r2-review.jsonl'}", "tier": 2, "pii": False}


def has_r2_sink():
    return any(s.get("name") == "r2-local" for s in sinks_of(read_config()))


def ensure_r2_sink(dry):
    """--no-sink's local tier-2 sink (docstring). Refuses beside a sink that leaves the Mac."""
    c = read_config()
    leaving = [str(s.get("name") or s.get("url")) for s in http_sinks(c) if not s.get("paused")]
    if leaving:
        return 1, (f"sink: no local sink written (--no-sink) — {', '.join(leaving)} is already configured and "
                   "events leave through it; `sessionpipe sink remove <name>` to keep them here")
    want = r2_sink()
    have = any(s == want for s in sinks_of(c))
    if not dry and not have:
        c["sinks"] = [s for s in sinks_of(c) if s.get("name") != "r2-local"] + [want]
        write_config(c)
    line = ("sink: r2-local at tier 2, already current" if have else
            f"sink: r2-local {'would be ' if dry else ''}written, tier 2, local")
    return 0, line + f" — events stay here, in {want['url'][5:]}"


def cmd_gate(dry, no_sink=False, sink=False):
    if not no_sink and not sink and has_r2_sink():
        say("r2-local is configured: staying local (R2's read is not done) — `sheep gate --sink` writes spacesheep")
        no_sink = True
    if not GATE.is_file():
        raise Refused(f"{GATE} does not exist — every hook behind it would exit 2; "
                      "launch the branch that adds it (or pull main) first")
    probe = subprocess.run([sys.executable, str(GATE)], input=b"{}", capture_output=True, timeout=20)
    if probe.returncode != 0:
        raise Refused(f"{GATE} exits {probe.returncode} on an empty event — nothing written")
    total = {"gated": 0, "ungated": 0, "absent": 0}
    hooked = False
    seed = seed_command()
    if seed and seed_missing(seed):
        raise Refused(f"{seed_missing(seed)} is missing — nothing written; reinstall sessionpipe, "
                      "then `sheep gate` at once (an install rewrites every entry ungated)")
    for d in claude_dirs():
        path = d / "settings.json"
        changes, s = gate_file(path, dry, seed)
        if s is None:
            continue
        c = counts(s)
        if c["gated"] or c["ungated"] or changes:
            hooked = True
            for k in total:
                total[k] += c[k]
        verb = "would change" if dry else "changed"
        say(f"{path}: {c['gated']} gated, {c['ungated']} ungated, {c['absent']} absent"
            + (f" — {verb}: {', '.join(changes)}" if changes else ""))
    if not hooked:
        say("sessionpipe is not installed here — `sessionpipe install --backfill 0` first (no sink yet), then `sheep gate`")
        return 1
    if total["ungated"] and not dry:
        raise Refused("an entry is still ungated after the write — no sink written")
    kept = ensure_kept(dry)  # before the forget and the sink: neither a refusal nor a missing key skips it
    if kept:
        say(kept)
    rc = cmd_forget(dry)
    if rc and not dry:
        say("sink: not written — a private session is still in the outbox")
        return rc
    if not no_sink:
        say(ensure_sink(dry))
        return rc
    r2rc, line = ensure_r2_sink(dry)
    say(line)
    return rc or r2rc


def hook_totals():
    """(totals, lines, files hooked, unreadable, dark) over every Claude config dir — check's body,
    and what hooks/sync.py reads at session start (R1). `dark`: config dirs sessionpipe never
    hooked while another is hooked — their sessions never report; counted only then, since with
    none hooked sessionpipe is simply not installed."""
    lines, total, files, unreadable = [], {"gated": 0, "ungated": 0, "absent": 0}, 0, 0
    dark = []
    for d in claude_dirs():
        path = d / "settings.json"
        try:
            cfg = read_settings(path)
        except (OSError, ValueError, Refused) as exc:
            lines.append(f"{path}: unreadable — {exc}")
            unreadable += 1
            continue
        if cfg is None:
            if (d / "projects").is_dir():
                dark.append(path)  # sessions run here and none report
            continue
        c = counts(survey(cfg))
        if not (c["gated"] or c["ungated"]):
            dark.append(path)
            continue
        files += 1
        for k in total:
            total[k] += c[k]
        lines.append(f"{path}: {c['gated']} gated, {c['ungated']} ungated, {c['absent']} absent")
    if not files:
        dark = []
    for path in dark:
        lines.append(f"{path}: never hooked — its sessions do not report (sheep gate adds them)")
    return total, lines, files, unreadable, dark


HTTP_URL = re.compile(r"https?://")


def http_sinks(c):
    """The sinks that leave the Mac (a `file:` sink stays on it)."""
    return [s for s in sinks_of(c) if HTTP_URL.match(str(s.get("url") or ""))]


def effective_tier(s):
    """The sink's tier capped by the receiver's max_tier; a max_tier of 0 is 0, not "unset"."""
    try:
        mt = s.get("max_tier")
        return min(int(s.get("tier") or 0), 3 if mt is None else int(mt))
    except (TypeError, ValueError):
        return None


def sink_problem(c):
    """Why config.json's sinks are not D1's — exactly one http(s) sink, spacesheep.dev, unpaused,
    at an effective tier of 2 or less — or None. No http sink at all is not a failure (nothing
    leaves: the R2 phase, a Mac with no key yet); check makes that a note."""
    leaving = http_sinks(c)
    if not leaving:
        return None
    others = [str(s.get("name") or s.get("url")) for s in leaving
              if s.get("name") != SINK["name"] or str(s.get("url") or "").rstrip("/") != SINK["url"]]
    if others or len(leaving) > 1:
        return (f"{len(leaving)} http sinks ({', '.join(str(s.get('name') or s.get('url')) for s in leaving)}) — "
                f"D1 is exactly one, {SINK['name']} at {SINK['url']}; `sessionpipe sink remove <name>` the rest")
    s = leaving[0]
    if s.get("paused"):
        return f"{SINK['name']} is PAUSED ({s['paused']}) — nothing reaches the board and no forget reaches it"
    tier = effective_tier(s)
    if tier is None or tier > SINK["tier"]:
        return f"{SINK['name']} at tier {tier if tier is not None else '?'} — above D1's {SINK['tier']}, tool input and output would leave"
    return None


def daemon_refusing():
    """True when sessionpipe's control daemon logged `refused (mode)` after its last start line."""
    try:
        lines = (state_dir().joinpath(*DAEMON_LOG)).read_text(encoding="utf-8", errors="replace").splitlines()
    except OSError:
        return False
    starts = [i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if DAEMON_UP.search(l)]
    return any("refused (mode)" in l for l in lines[(starts[-1] + 1) if starts else 0:])


def r2_leftover():
    """A line when the R2 day's file is still on disk with no r2-local sink to need it, or is
    readable by others while one does; else None."""
    f = Path(r2_sink()["url"][len("file:"):])
    try:
        st = f.stat()
    except OSError:
        return None
    mode = st.st_mode & 0o777
    if not has_r2_sink():
        return (f"{f} is still here ({st.st_size / 1e6:.1f} MB of tier-2 turn text, mode {mode:o}) with no "
                f"r2-local sink — R2's read is done; `rm` it (`gate --sink` would have)")
    if mode != 0o600:
        return f"{f} is mode {mode:o}, not 600 — its turn text is readable by other users; chmod 600 it"
    return None


def cmd_check():
    """First line is the summary bootstrap.sh --check prints; exit 1 on anything ungated, an
    unreadable settings file, a config dir never hooked, a private session in the outbox, sinks
    other than D1's (sink_problem), update_check not false, or a control daemon with a private
    folder, a stale plist or a name the tab does not know. Notes never fail it: counted in the
    first line, each printed below (bootstrap.sh shows them on a pass too) — the R2 file left
    behind, no http sink at all, a refusing control daemon."""
    total, lines, files, unreadable, dark = hook_totals()
    priv = private_sessions()
    cfg = read_config() if files else {}
    sink_bad = sink_problem(cfg) if files else None
    update_on = bool(files) and cfg.get("update_check") is not False
    notes = [r2_leftover()]
    if files and not http_sinks(cfg):
        notes.append(f"no {SINK['name']} sink — nothing leaves this Mac and its sessions do not reach the board "
                     "(D1 wants one: `sheep gate --sink` once R2's read is done)")
    if daemon_refusing():
        notes.append("the control daemon refused a headless turn (mode) since its last start — sessionpipe "
                     f"0.5.0 keeps refusing after one failed `claude --help` read; restart it: {DAEMON_KICK}")
    notes = [n for n in notes if n]
    try:
        cs = control_state()
        clines, cprob = control_lines(cs)
        cpaired = cs["paired"]
    except Refused as exc:
        clines, cprob, cpaired = [], [f"control: {exc}"], True  # an unreadable control.json is worth saying
    if not files and not cpaired:
        clines = []  # sessionpipe not installed and never paired: nothing to say
    if not files:
        head = "sessionpipe hooks: none installed"
    else:
        head = f"sessionpipe hooks: {total['gated']} gated"
        if total["ungated"]:
            head += f", {total['ungated']} UNGATED — run {_sheep_cmd()} gate"
        if dark:
            head += (f", {len(dark)} login dir{'' if len(dark) == 1 else 's'} NEVER HOOKED — "
                     f"its sessions do not report; run {_sheep_cmd()} gate")
        if total["absent"]:
            head += f", {total['absent']} absent (sheep gate adds them)"
    if unreadable:
        head += f", {unreadable} settings file(s) UNREADABLE"
    if priv:
        head += f", {len(priv)} PRIVATE session(s) in the outbox"
    if sink_bad:
        head += ", sinks WRONG"
    if update_on:
        head += ", update_check ON"
    if cprob:
        head += f", control: {len(cprob)} problem{'' if len(cprob) == 1 else 's'}"
    if notes:
        head += f", {len(notes)} note(s)"
    say(head)
    for line in lines + (sink_lines() if files else []) + clines + cprob:
        say("  " + line)
    if priv:
        say(f"  outbox: {len(priv)} private session(s) — run {_sheep_cmd()} forget-private")
    if sink_bad:
        say(f"  sinks: {sink_bad}")
    if update_on:
        say(f"  update_check is {json.dumps(cfg.get('update_check', True))} in {config_file()} — sessionpipe 0.6+ "
            f"updates itself and re-runs `install`, which ungates every entry; {_sheep_cmd()} gate sets it false")
    if files and cfg.get("machine") != machine_name():
        say(f"  machine is {json.dumps(cfg.get('machine'))}, not {json.dumps(machine_name())} — the board names this Mac "
            "by its DHCP hostname meanwhile; sheep gate sets it")
    for n in notes:
        say("  note: " + n)
    return 1 if total["ungated"] or unreadable or dark or priv or sink_bad or update_on or cprob else 0


def cmd_forget(dry):
    priv = private_sessions()
    if not priv:
        say("outbox: no private session")
        return 0
    if dry:
        for sid, why in priv:
            say(f"would forget {sid} ({why})")
        return 0
    sp = sessionpipe_bin()
    if not sp:
        say(f"outbox: {len(priv)} private session(s), and no sessionpipe binary to forget them with")
        return 1
    paused = [s.get("name") for s in sinks_of(read_config()) if s.get("paused")]
    if paused:  # sessionpipe skips a paused sink silently, then deletes the outbox file anyway
        say(f"outbox: {len(priv)} private session(s), and sink(s) {', '.join(map(str, paused))} paused — "
            "a forget would never reach them; unpause first (`sessionpipe sink list`)")
        return 1
    rc, pending = 0, read_pending()
    for sid, why in priv:
        pending[sid] = why
        write_pending(pending)  # before the call: sessionpipe deletes the outbox file either way
        try:
            r = subprocess.run([sp, "forget", "claude-code", sid], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=60)
            out, code = r.stdout + r.stderr, r.returncode
        except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
            out, code = "timed out after 60 s", 1
        ok = code == 0 and "✗" not in out
        if ok:
            pending.pop(sid, None)
            write_pending(pending)
        say(f"{'forgot' if ok else 'FAILED to forget (kept pending, retried next run)'} {sid} ({why})")
        for line in out.splitlines():
            say("  " + line.strip())
        rc |= 0 if ok else 1
    return rc


def board_sessions():
    """Every session spacesheep.dev holds, both Macs', through the CLI's own `sessions list`
    (read-only; its JSON is {sessions: [...], next_offset: N | null}, cwd `~`-relative)."""
    ss = spacesheep_bin()
    if not ss:
        raise Refused("no spacesheep CLI on PATH — nothing to read the board with")
    rows, offset = [], 0
    for _ in range(AUDIT_MAX_PAGES):
        try:
            r = subprocess.run([ss, "sessions", "list", "--limit", str(AUDIT_PAGE), "--offset", str(offset)],
                               capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=60)
        except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
            raise Refused(f"spacesheep sessions list --offset {offset} timed out after 60 s")
        if r.returncode:
            raise Refused(f"spacesheep sessions list --offset {offset} exited {r.returncode}: "
                          + ((r.stderr or r.stdout).strip().splitlines() or [""])[-1])
        try:
            page = json.loads(r.stdout)
        except ValueError:
            raise Refused(f"spacesheep sessions list --offset {offset} printed no JSON")
        got = [s for s in page.get("sessions") or [] if isinstance(s, dict)] if isinstance(page, dict) else []
        rows += got
        nxt = page.get("next_offset") if isinstance(page, dict) else None
        if not got or not isinstance(nxt, int) or nxt <= offset:
            return rows
        offset = nxt
    raise Refused(f"more than {AUDIT_MAX_PAGES * AUDIT_PAGE} sessions — stopped paging; raise AUDIT_MAX_PAGES")


def cmd_audit():
    """Read-only: every board session whose cwd the gate calls private, i.e. one that leaked (or
    left before the gate knew its folder). Exit 1 on a hit, 0 on none."""
    rows = board_sessions()
    hits = []
    for s in rows:
        cwd = s.get("cwd") if isinstance(s.get("cwd"), str) else None
        why = _gate.private_reason(cwd=cwd) if cwd else None
        if why:
            hits.append((s, why))
    for s, why in hits:
        say(f"PRIVATE on the board: {s.get('source')}:{s.get('session_id')} on {s.get('machine')}, cwd {s.get('cwd')} ({why})")
    say(f"board: {len(rows)} session(s) read, {len(hits)} private"
        + (" — the deletion is `sessionpipe forget claude-code <id>` per session, run by the owner" if hits else ""))
    return 1 if hits else 0


def _get(url, headers=None, timeout=15):
    req = urllib.request.Request(url, headers=headers or {})
    try:
        with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=timeout) as r:
            return r.status, r.read()
    except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:
        return e.code, b""
    except Exception as e:
        return 0, str(e).encode()


def receiver_status():
    """[(ok, line)]: the container image under each name and the npm package, all read anonymously."""
    out = []
    for image in RECEIVER_IMAGES:
        st, body = _get(f"https://ghcr.io/token?scope=repository:{image}:pull")
        tok = ""
        try:
            tok = json.loads(body).get("token", "") if st == 200 else ""
        except ValueError:
            pass
        st, _ = _get(f"https://ghcr.io/v2/{image}/manifests/latest", {
            "Authorization": f"Bearer {tok}",
            "Accept": "application/vnd.oci.image.index.v1+json, application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.v2+json"})
        out.append((st == 200, f"image ghcr.io/{image}:latest: "
                    + ("pullable" if st == 200 else f"not pullable anonymously (HTTP {st})")))
    st, body = _get(f"https://registry.npmjs.org/{RECEIVER_NPM}/latest")
    try:
        meta = json.loads(body) if st == 200 else {}
    except ValueError:
        meta = {}
    if not meta.get("version"):
        out.append((False, f"npm {RECEIVER_NPM}: not found (HTTP {st})"))
        return out
    st, tgz = _get(meta.get("dist", {}).get("tarball", ""), timeout=30)
    cli = ""
    try:
        with tarfile.open(fileobj=io.BytesIO(tgz), mode="r:gz") as t:
            cli = t.extractfile("package/dist/cli.js").read().decode("utf-8", "replace")
    except Exception:
        pass
    placeholder = "lands in a later milestone" in cli   # sessionpipe's own words, matched as it prints them
    out.append((bool(cli) and not placeholder, f"npm {RECEIVER_NPM} {meta['version']}: "
                + ("a placeholder — its CLI says the receiver lands in a later milestone" if placeholder
                   else "has a CLI — read its README before step 7" if cli else "no dist/cli.js in the tarball")))
    return out


def cmd_receiver_check():
    res = receiver_status()
    for ok, line in res:
        say(("ok  " if ok else "--  ") + line)
    if any(ok for ok, _ in res):
        say("a receiver exists upstream: step 7 (E4) can write `sheep receiver` and the home server's README")
        return 0
    say("no receiver to run yet: step 7 waits on upstream (proposal W6, R8)")
    return 1


def cmd_receiver():
    cmd_receiver_check()
    say("sheep receiver: not built — step 7 (E4) writes its run line from the receiver's own docs, "
        "through the home server's tier gate")
    return 1


# --- the control daemon (docs/session-listen-2026-10-13.md, B1) --------------------------------
#
# What sessionpipe does that this follows (its 0.5.0 cli.js, read 2026-10-15):
# - control.json sits beside config.json (`controlFile`), 0600, {name, folders, mode, receivers,
#   limits?}; a receiver may hold its token. This rewrites only `name` and `folders` and keeps
#   every other key byte-for-byte as JSON, written the way `writePrivate` does (tmp, rename, 0600).
# - The daemon watches the file every 5 s and swaps in the new config (`reload`): its folder test
#   (`allowed`, a real-path prefix, so a repo's worktrees are inside it) changes at once. The
#   receiver hears the name and folders only in a hello, every 10 min (`HELLO_EVERY_MS`), and
#   `reload` sends none — so a changed name restarts the agent (`launchctl kickstart -k`), the
#   fix the laptop's name trap needed (section 8).
# - A session's spacesheep page names its machine by `machineName`: config.json's `machine`,
#   else the hostname minus .local/.lan/.home. `pair` names the daemon `--name`, else the existing
#   control.json's `name`, else config.json's `machine`, else os.hostname() with the suffix (cli.js
#   ~5608; pair() ~5202 keeps cfg.name), so a re-pair keeps the name; only a first pair with no
#   `--name` and no `machine` takes the hostname, and the tab then says "<Mac> isn't listening
#   yet" — so the name written here is machineName's rule, ported.
# - The plist (`serviceFiles`) runs `<node> <cli.js> control run`, cli.js by its real path; it
#   is not repaired by `install` or `update` (README, L8). A plist whose cli is not the installed
#   one, or whose node is gone, is stale: only `pair` again (a passkey tap) rewrites it.
CONTROL_LABEL = "org.sessionpipe.control"
CONTROL_RECEIVER = "spacesheep.dev"


def control_file():
    return config_file().parent / "control.json"


def read_control():
    """control.json as a dict, None when absent; Refused when unreadable (never rewritten)."""
    f = control_file()
    if not f.exists():
        return None
    try:
        c = json.loads(f.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
    except (OSError, ValueError) as exc:
        raise Refused(f"{f} is unreadable ({exc}) — not touched")
    if not isinstance(c, dict):
        raise Refused(f"{f} is not a JSON object — not touched")
    return c


def write_control(c):
    f = control_file()
    tmp = f.with_name(f"{f.name}.{os.getpid()}.tmp")
    fd = os.open(tmp, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_TRUNC, 0o600)
    with os.fdopen(fd, "w", encoding="utf-8") as fh:
        fh.write(json.dumps(c, indent=2) + "\n")
    os.chmod(tmp, 0o600)
    os.replace(tmp, f)


def paired(c):
    return isinstance(c, dict) and isinstance(c.get("receivers"), list) and len(c["receivers"]) > 0


def control_name():
    """What this Mac's sessions register under on spacesheep — sessionpipe's machineName, which is
    config.json's `machine`. `gate` writes that key from machine_name() (2026-10-16), so before a
    gate has run the daemon takes the name the gate will write, and check's machine line says
    the sessions lag; never os.hostname(), the DHCP name that split the board."""
    try:
        m = read_config().get("machine")
    except Refused:
        m = None
    return str(m)[:80] if m else machine_name()


def projects_root():
    return Path(os.environ.get("SHEEP_PROJECTS") or HOME / "projects")


def folder_private(path):
    """Why a folder may never be in control.json, or None. An allow-list (review gate S1, 2026-10-16):
    a folder whose real path lies inside projects_root() — a repo, a repo group, a folder in one —
    and none of hooks/sheep_gate.py's private, the one definition (PRIVATE_REPOS as a path part,
    case-folded; _secrets; ~/projects, ~ and their ancestors), for the folder itself; nor a
    PRIVATE_REPOS repo inside it (the gate's broad rule knows only the real ~/projects, not
    $SHEEP_PROJECTS); nor, for a folder that is no repo itself (films, oss, taken whole), a private
    name among its subfolders to depth 3. The deny-list alone passed a folder that CONTAINS Drive's
    _secrets — the vault's parent, ~/Library — and the daemon's allowed() is a real-path prefix, so
    a session could have started anywhere below it."""
    why = _gate.private_reason(str(path))
    if why:
        return why
    root = projects_root()
    if not covers([root], path):
        return f"{path} is not inside {root}: the daemon runs sessions only in the repos there"
    if os.path.realpath(str(path)) == os.path.realpath(str(root)):
        return f"{path} is {root} whole, and with it every private repo"
    try:
        for name in _gate.PRIVATE_REPOS:
            inner = root / name
            if inner.exists() and covers([str(path)], inner):
                return f"{path} holds {inner}"
    except OSError:
        pass
    if not os.path.lexists(os.path.join(str(path), ".git")):
        hit = _private_below(str(path), 3)
        if hit:
            return f"{path} holds {hit}, a folder with a private name"
    return None


def _private_below(top, depth):
    """The first folder or link under top, at most depth levels down, whose name is private
    (sheep_gate.private_part), else None. scandir, symlinks never followed (the daemon judges a
    session's real path, so a link out of the group is not inside it, and a loop is not walked);
    a repo's .git and node_modules are not descended — the cost is a few hundred entries a group."""
    stack = [(top, 1)]
    while stack:
        d, level = stack.pop()
        try:
            with os.scandir(d) as it:
                entries = list(it)
        except OSError:
            continue
        for e in entries:
            try:
                is_dir = e.is_dir(follow_symlinks=False)
                link = e.is_symlink()
            except OSError:
                continue
            if (is_dir or link) and _gate.private_part(e.name):
                return e.path
            if is_dir and level < depth and e.name not in (".git", "node_modules"):
                stack.append((e.path, level + 1))
    return None


def covers(folders, path):
    """path lies under one of folders by real path, as the daemon's allowed() decides."""
    try:
        r = os.path.realpath(str(path))
    except OSError:
        return False
    for f in folders:
        rf = os.path.realpath(str(f))
        if r == rf or r.startswith(rf.rstrip(os.sep) + os.sep):
            return True
    return False


def repo_folders():
    """Every folder sessions may run in: each child of ~/projects that is a git repo, or that
    holds repos (films, oss — taken whole), bar the private and guarded ones. Sorted by name."""
    out, root = [], projects_root()
    try:
        kids = sorted(root.iterdir(), key=lambda p: p.name.casefold())
    except OSError:
        return []
    for d in kids:
        if not d.is_dir() or d.name.startswith("."):
            continue
        # a repo or group first, so a folder with no repo (tmp) costs no private walk
        if ((d / ".git").exists() or any((s / ".git").exists() for s in _subdirs(d))) and not folder_private(d):
            out.append(str(d))
    return out


def _subdirs(d):
    try:
        return [s for s in d.iterdir() if s.is_dir() and not s.name.startswith(".")]
    except OSError:
        return []


def launch_agent():
    return Path(os.environ.get("SHEEP_LAUNCH_AGENTS") or HOME / "Library" / "LaunchAgents") / f"{CONTROL_LABEL}.plist"


def plist_stale():
    """Why the daemon's plist will not run the installed sessionpipe, None when it will, '' when
    there is no plist (pair --no-service, or not paired)."""
    import plistlib
    f = launch_agent()
    if not f.exists():
        return ""
    try:
        args = plistlib.loads(f.read_bytes()).get("ProgramArguments") or []
    except Exception as exc:
        return f"{f} is unreadable ({exc})"
    if len(args) < 2:
        return f"{f} names no cli"
    node, cli = str(args[0]), str(args[1])
    if not os.path.exists(node):
        return f"its node {node} is gone"
    sp = sessionpipe_bin()
    if not sp:
        return "sessionpipe is not installed"
    if os.path.realpath(cli) != os.path.realpath(sp):
        return f"it runs {cli}, not the installed {os.path.realpath(sp)}"
    return None


def control_state():
    """One read of the control side, for check, sync.py and control itself."""
    c = read_control()
    s = {"paired": paired(c), "conf": c, "name": control_name()}
    if not s["paired"]:
        return s
    folders = [f for f in c.get("folders") or [] if isinstance(f, str)]
    s["folders"] = folders
    whys = [(f, folder_private(f)) for f in folders]  # once a folder: the group walk is not free
    s["private"] = [(f, why) for f, why in whys if why]
    s["missing"] = [f for f in folders if not os.path.isdir(f)]
    s["unlisted"] = [Path(f).name for f in repo_folders() if not covers(folders, f)]
    s["stale"] = plist_stale()
    s["misnamed"] = c.get("name") != s["name"]
    return s


def receivers_text(c):
    out = []
    for r in c.get("receivers") or []:
        if isinstance(r, dict):
            host = re.sub(r"^https?://", "", str(r.get("url") or r.get("control") or "?")).split("/")[0]
            out.append(f"{host} (machine {r.get('machine', '?')})")
    return ", ".join(out) or "none"


def control_notes():
    """sync.py's start note on a paired Mac: a repo the daemon cannot run a session in, a stale
    plist, a private folder, a name the tab does not know. Quiet when unpaired or all is well."""
    s = control_state()
    if not s["paired"]:
        return []
    out = []
    if s["private"]:
        out.append(f"⚠ sessionpipe control: private folder{'s' if len(s['private']) > 1 else ''} "
                   f"{', '.join(f for f, _ in s['private'])} — run {HERE / 'sheep'} control")
    if s["unlisted"]:
        out.append(f"sessionpipe control: {', '.join(s['unlisted'])} not in its folders, so the Session tab "
                   f"cannot reach {'it' if len(s['unlisted']) == 1 else 'them'} — run {HERE / 'sheep'} control")
    if s["misnamed"]:
        out.append(f"⚠ sessionpipe control is named {s['conf'].get('name')!r}, this Mac's sessions {s['name']!r}: "
                   f"the tab says it isn't listening — run {HERE / 'sheep'} control")
    if s["stale"]:
        out.append(f"⚠ sessionpipe control daemon is stale ({s['stale']}): the owner re-pairs it, a passkey tap — "
                   f"{pair_line(s['name'], [], s['conf'].get('mode', 'safe'))}")
    return out


def control_lines(s):
    """(lines, problems) for check: problems fail it — a private folder, a stale plist, a name the
    tab does not know; the rest is said and passes."""
    if not s["paired"]:
        return ["control: not paired here (sheep control prints the pair line)"], []
    c, lines, problems = s["conf"], [], []
    lines.append(f"control: paired as {c.get('name')}, mode {c.get('mode', 'safe')}, "
                 f"{len(s['folders'])} folders, receivers {receivers_text(c)}")
    for f, why in s["private"]:
        problems.append(f"control folder PRIVATE: {f} — {why}; run {_sheep_cmd()} control")
    if s["misnamed"]:
        problems.append(f"control named {c.get('name')!r} but this Mac's sessions register as {s['name']!r}: "
                        f"the tab says it isn't listening — run {_sheep_cmd()} control")
    if s["stale"]:
        problems.append(f"control daemon STALE: {s['stale']} — re-pair (sessionpipe control pair "
                        f"{CONTROL_RECEIVER} --mode {c.get('mode', 'safe')} --name {s['name']}: the owner's, a passkey tap)")
    if s["stale"] == "":
        lines.append("control: no launchd agent — the daemon runs only by hand (`sessionpipe control run`)")
    if s["missing"]:
        lines.append(f"control folder missing: {', '.join(s['missing'])} (sheep control drops it)")
    if s["unlisted"]:
        lines.append(f"control: not in its folders: {', '.join(s['unlisted'])} (sheep control adds them)")
    return lines, problems


def pair_line(name, folders, mode="auto"):
    """The line the owner pastes: every value shell-quoted (a folder may hold a space)."""
    q = shlex.quote
    return " ".join([f"sessionpipe control pair {CONTROL_RECEIVER} --mode {q(mode)} --name {q(name)}"] +
                    [f"--folder {q(f)}" for f in folders])


def cmd_control(dry, adds):
    """Write control.json's folders and name from this Mac's repos; refuse a private folder."""
    for a in adds:
        p = os.path.abspath(os.path.expanduser(a))
        why = folder_private(p)
        if why:
            raise Refused(f"refused: {why} — a private folder never goes into control.json")
        if not os.path.isdir(p):
            raise Refused(f"refused: {p} is not a folder")
    want = repo_folders()
    c, name = read_control(), control_name()
    if not paired(c):
        say("control: not paired on this Mac. The owner pairs it in an attended session (a passkey tap, link valid 10 min; an agent's run is denied):")
        extra = [os.path.abspath(os.path.expanduser(a)) for a in adds]
        say("  " + pair_line(name, want + [p for p in extra if not covers(want, p)]))
        return 1
    old = [f for f in c.get("folders") or [] if isinstance(f, str)]
    # by real path, as the daemon's allowed() reads them: an old folder inside a wanted one, or the
    # same folder spelled another way, is covered already and dropped
    keep = [f for f in old if not covers(want, f) and os.path.isdir(f) and not folder_private(f)]
    new = want + keep
    for a in adds:
        p = os.path.abspath(os.path.expanduser(a))
        if not covers(new, p):
            new.append(p)
    dropped = [f for f in old if f not in new]
    added = [f for f in new if f not in old]
    renamed = c.get("name") != name
    say(f"control: paired with {receivers_text(c)}, mode {c.get('mode', 'safe')}")
    say(f"  name: {name}" + (f" (was {c.get('name')!r})" if renamed else ""))
    say(f"  folders: {len(new)}" + (f", added {', '.join(Path(f).name for f in added)}" if added else "")
        + (f", dropped {', '.join(dropped)}" if dropped else ""))
    if not (added or dropped or renamed):
        say("  nothing to change")
        return 0
    if dry:
        say("  (dry run: nothing written)")
        return 0
    c["folders"], c["name"] = new, name
    write_control(c)
    say(f"  wrote {control_file()} — the daemon reloads it within 5 s")
    if renamed and plist_stale() is None:
        lc = os.environ.get("SHEEP_LAUNCHCTL") or "launchctl"
        r = subprocess.run([lc, "kickstart", "-k", f"gui/{os.getuid()}/{CONTROL_LABEL}"],
                           capture_output=True, text=True)
        say("  restarted the daemon so its hello carries the name" if r.returncode == 0 else
            f"  the daemon did not restart ({(r.stderr or r.stdout).strip() or r.returncode}): "
            f"launchctl kickstart -k gui/{os.getuid()}/{CONTROL_LABEL}")
    return 0


def main(argv):
    if not argv or argv[0] in ("-h", "--help", "help"):
        say(__doc__.split("\n\n")[1] if argv else __doc__)
        return 0 if argv else 2
    verb, rest = argv[0], argv[1:]
    if verb == "url":
        if not rest:
            say("sheep url: give one or more links")
            return 2
        port = mirror_port()
        for u in rest:
            say(chat_url(u, port))
        return 0
    if verb not in FLAGS:
        say(f"sheep: unknown verb {verb!r} — sheep --help")
        return 2
    adds = []
    if verb == "control":  # --folder takes a value
        left = []
        it = iter(rest)
        for a in it:
            if a == "--folder":
                v = next(it, None)
                if not v:
                    say("sheep control: --folder needs a folder")
                    return 2
                adds.append(v)
            else:
                left.append(a)
        rest = left
    extra = [a for a in rest if a not in FLAGS[verb]]
    if extra:
        say(f"sheep {verb}: unknown argument(s) {' '.join(extra)} — sheep --help")
        return 2
    dry, no_sink = "--dry-run" in rest, "--no-sink" in rest
    if verb == "gate" and no_sink and "--sink" in rest:
        say("sheep gate: --no-sink and --sink together — pick one")
        return 2
    try:
        return {"gate": lambda: cmd_gate(dry, no_sink, "--sink" in rest), "check": cmd_check, "forget-private": lambda: cmd_forget(dry),
                "audit": cmd_audit, "receiver-check": cmd_receiver_check, "receiver": cmd_receiver,
                "control": lambda: cmd_control(dry, adds)}[verb]()
    except Exception as exc:  # Refused, claude-settings' lock, a bad file: one line, never a traceback
        say(f"sheep {verb}: {exc}")
        return 1


if __name__ == "__main__":
    import signal
    signal.signal(signal.SIGPIPE, signal.SIG_DFL)  # `sheep check | head -1` ends quietly
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
